  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Ghanaians carry an English or Christian first name (Emmanuel, Abigail) or a Muslim one (Ibrahim, Fatima), a day name and a family name. Akan day names say which day you were born: Kwasi and Akosua on Sunday, Kwadwo and Adwoa on Monday, Kwabena and Abena on Tuesday, Kwaku and Akua on Wednesday, Yaw and Yaa on Thursday, Kofi and Afua on Friday, Kwame and Ama on Saturday (Fante spellings differ: Esi, Ekua, Ekow, Kweku, Efua). Ga names mark birth order and twins, and Ga royals and elders are addressed as Nii (men) and Naa (women). Ewe day names are close to the Akan ones (Kofi, Kodzo, Kwaku, Yawo, Afi, Ama). Family names are often the father's or chosen from the family's line.",
